          <p>Sustainable climate action requires not just strong policy frameworks, but capable leadership at the local level. In India's rural governance systems, block and district-level officers—often referred to as middle managers—play a critical role in implementing programs, mobilizing communities, and responding to local challenges. However, these individuals often operate in complex environments with limited resources, competing priorities, and high levels of administrative pressure.</p>
          <p>The School of Climate and Sustainability believes that building the leadership, confidence, and systems-thinking capacity of these officials is essential to transforming service delivery and fostering climate resilience from the ground up.</p>
